                <pb facs="0974" n="854" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg854"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/231: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-08T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1922—3
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>114. Your telegram No. 114 of March 24, 5 p.m. Some time ago the Department
                    communicated to Mr. Schwerin, who has been ill, the substance of that telegram.
                    With his engineers he is in New York conducting negotiations for traffic
                    agreements and arranging other matters which are necessary incidental to the
                    carrying out of the contract of the Federal Telegraph Company. Exact information
                    will be cabled to you as soon as the Department can obtain it from Mr.
                    Schwerin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
